(REASON FOR ADMISSION) Tj T*
(The patient, a 34-year-old female, was admitted with acute right iliac fossa pain, nausea,) Tj T*
(and low-grade fever consistent with acute appendicitis.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(INVESTIGATIONS ON ADMISSION) Tj T*
(- WBC: 14.2 x10^9/L \(elevated\)) Tj T*
(- CRP: 87 mg/L \(elevated\)) Tj T*
(- Ultrasound abdomen: Non-compressible appendix, diameter 9mm, periappendiceal fat stranding) Tj T*
(- CT abdomen/pelvis: Confirmed acute appendicitis, no perforation or abscess) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(PROCEDURE PERFORMED) Tj T*
(Laparoscopic appendicectomy performed on May 6, 2024 under general anaesthesia.) Tj T*
(Operative findings: Acutely inflamed appendix, no perforation. Procedure uncomplicated.) Tj T*
(Specimen sent for histopathology.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(POSTOPERATIVE COURSE) Tj T*
(The patient recovered well. Oral intake resumed on postoperative day 1. Pain managed with) Tj T*
(paracetamol and ibuprofen. No wound complications. Afebrile at discharge.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(DISCHARGE MEDICATIONS) Tj T*
(1. Paracetamol 1g every 6 hours as needed for 5 days) Tj T*
(2. Ibuprofen 400mg every 8 hours with food for 3 days) Tj T*
(3. No antibiotics required \(uncomplicated case\)) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(FOLLOW-UP INSTRUCTIONS) Tj T*
(- Review with GP in 1 week for wound check) Tj T*
(- Return to emergency if fever >38.5C, increasing pain, or wound discharge) Tj T*
(- Histopathology results to be reviewed at outpatient appointment in 2 weeks) Tj T*
(- Avoid strenuous activity for 2 weeks; may return to desk work after 5 days) Tj T*
